Description: fast and simple Node.js version manager
 fnm (Fast Node Manager) installs Node.js versions and switches between
 them. It is a single native binary that covers the everyday nvm commands:
 install, use, default, list, exec and uninstall work as their nvm
 counterparts, and .nvmrc, .node-version and the package.json engines
 field are all read.
 .
 Shell integration comes from eval "$(fnm env)" in the shell's startup
 file; with --use-on-cd the Node.js version switches automatically on
 entering a directory. Completions for bash, zsh and fish are included.
